id: pm-csv-bounded-admission
title: Admit large CSV imports within declared memory and mutation budgets
description: "Stream initial or full validation before import commitment. Acceptance: a million-row fixture stays under a declared heap cap independent of file size; invalid final rows prevent atomic application; exact counts are distinguished from upper bounds. Reuse CSV mapping and SDK schema/status/transaction capabilities rather than introducing a dialect or journal."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T03:16:17.816Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T09:52:33.716Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Bounded million-row validation; late invalid rows cause zero atomic writes; exact and bounded estimates; typed SDK and compact CLI; no-git real-data validation; seeded state tests and npm/Bun release gates
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T03:17:36.890Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core public SDK exposes schema/status registries, complete reads and mutation/transaction primitives but no streaming CSV resource admission contract. pm-csv already owns parsing, mapping, schema negotiation and atomic import; pm-beads owns JSONL reconciliation and pm-todos owns todo files. This change adds bounded initial/full resource receipts and an opt-in atomic admission guard, reusing shared row validation. No dialect or journal is introduced. Workspace transactions do not isolate ordinary writers; existing per-write SDK rereads remain required and the final read/write window remains documented."
  "2026-10-29T03:29:52.640Z",codex-agent,"Implemented read-only csv admit and typed admitCSV with exact full counts, conservative initial lower bounds, mutation upper bounds, fixed field/record/column allocations, SHA-256 source binding and settings drift refusal. Atomic import can opt into the same full pass with --admission; only bounded bytes are materialized and source drift refuses before parsing. Targeted regressions cover late invalid rows, custom status normalization, finite limit fuzzing, all parser split points and every source/settings admission boundary. Million-row fixture is 163000015 bytes; final heap-cap rerun is pending."
  "2026-10-29T03:50:32.261Z",codex-agent,"Measured public origin/main tracker in a scratch non-git directory: 133 items, 133 exported/admitted rows, 46572 CSV bytes, zero invalid rows, maximum field width 2946 code units; full scan 47 ms and 57801136 bytes observed heap. Warmed only SDK-derived caches before making the copy read-only; all tracked bytes and all copied file hashes remained unchanged during measurement. Million-row fixture: 163000015 source bytes under --max-old-space-size=96 --max-semi-space-size=4, V8 heap limit 113246208 bytes (below declared 128 MiB), observed heap about 31.5 MB. Added revision-bound admitted steps, current SDK history checks including ABA, certified SDK list reads and source/settings interleaving tests; ordinary-writer final read/write window remains explicit."
  "2026-10-29T05:11:32.568Z",codex-agent,"Completed native admitted-write hardening: explicit SDK identities and revision-bound steps, deterministic peer identity adoption, per-invocation write counts, SDK semantic preview before any target application, source-based scope selection shared with legacy import, and configured-status filter normalization. Tests cover ordinary writers at inspection/capture/apply boundaries, keyed-creation races, peer edits during compensation, ABA replays, deleted targets, malformed retained bindings, all status roles and an empty executable PATH. Initial observation counts blank records toward its budget and remains non-authorizing at EOF. Public minimum SDK artifact 2026.8.20 has complete reads and status roles but lacks semantic preview and transaction-key derivation; read-only admission remains supported, while admitted application returns a typed upgrade remedy on such hosts. No dependency pin was changed."
  "2026-10-29T06:11:17.637Z",codex-agent,"Verification: the linked pm test command was run through pm test --run --progress --timeout 900 --shared-host-safe --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run: 25 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled, including 500 seeded sequences and 2000 operations. Automatic test evidence recording is disabled by the existing project policy, so the result is recorded here without changing settings. A subsequent focused admission/parser/atomic/command regression run passed 165 tests with zero skips; admission.ts measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, docstrings and duplication checks passed. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-29T06:11:55.600Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof used a disposable non-git copy, never the reviewed checkout. The fixed baseline passed both selected regressions; removing only StreamingCSVParser.appendField allocation guards made the field/record resource test fail, and disabling only importCSV admission dispatch made the late-invalid-row zero-write test fail. Restoring each implementation made its selected regression pass again. The reviewed source hashes stayed unchanged. Refreshed overlap against the public 2026.10.28 SDK found only in-memory mutation parsing/document resolution, no streaming admission surface; sibling package and upstream issue searches found no duplicate contract. Final read-only public tracker measurement: 133 items and exact rows, 46572 CSV bytes, zero invalid rows, maximum field width 2946 code units, mutation upper bound 133, 52 ms, 44049096 bytes observed heap; all copied file hashes unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T06:22:11.117Z",codex-agent,"Expanded state evidence passed: 500 seeded operation sequences, 2000 operations, 386 exports and 48 complete export/import/replay round trips. Every comparison reads actual native SDK state against independent SDK reference transitions; peer edits after replay refuse older inputs and retain relationships/scope. Packed validation exposed a known older-host preview limitation: SDK 2026.10.25 treats installed dependency links as tracker storage, while a fresh packed CLI install and guarded application succeed on the current 2026.10.28 host. The public preview signature accepts only pmRoot/transactionId/author/mutations and no storage-exclusion override; no custom snapshot or validation bypass is added. Added an actionable typed host/storage remedy, retained the dependency pin, and expanded packed acceptance to npm/Bun current project-local, global and npx/bunx contexts. Strict health passes with an isolated global package registry; the ambient registry reports an unrelated pm-github host-version skew."
  "2026-10-29T06:28:16.477Z",codex-agent,"Final local acceptance: npm run accept:packed passed all nine scenarios. Six current 2026.10.28 contexts (npm/Bun project-local, npm/Bun global, npx and bunx) completed guarded native application and importer replay with zero new replay writes. The three legacy/minimum-host contexts passed their existing package acceptance and read-only admission; guarded application returned the typed upgrade remedy with no target created. The final native-validation/remedy regression passed 1/1. Dependency and 100% coverage thresholds are unchanged. Implementation, docs, public-copy metrics, state property evidence and behavioral revert proof are ready for review; full npm and Bun release gates remain delegated to the exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-29T06:47:44.111Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/40829522381 at 3a1bb71: Node 22 completed 433 tests, all passed with zero skips; all source lines/functions reached 100%, but aggregate branches were 99.92% (index.ts 99.80%), so the unchanged release gate correctly failed before packed/Bun stages. The focused branch receipt identifies redundant autoMap/skipHeaders fallback arms after strict admission had already captured both booleans. Removed those unreachable defaults without changing normalized transaction identities; replay/dry-run checks, typecheck and lint are being verified before a fresh exact-head CI run. No threshold was lowered."
  "2026-10-29T06:47:57.420Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up verification passed: npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern \"admitted atomic replay|admitted keyed creates\" test/admission.test.ts (2/2 passed, zero skips); npm run lint. The correction only removes redundant defaults from already-normalized admitted transaction inputs. The ready PR is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/pull/213; final exact-head npm/Bun CI remains pending and can be followed from the PR checks. All final tracker writes precede the next CI head."
  "2026-10-29T07:18:36.100Z",codex-agent,"CI handoff under the 30-minute monitoring rule: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/40831558404 validates implementation head 10678a7. At the final poll, the Node 26 full npm release gate passed at unchanged 100% line/branch/function thresholds; its Bun gate was running. Node 22 npm was running and Bun had not started. Current job logs remain unavailable until job completion, so no unobserved final test counts are claimed. The prior implementation attempt completed 433 tests per runtime with zero failures/skips but failed the branch threshold; the redundant defaults were corrected and replay/dry-run checks passed. This tracker-only handoff changes no implementation; its final head still requires fresh CI. The feature remains open, my claim is released, and closure belongs to the orchestrator. No merge or publication was performed."
  "2026-10-29T08:33:06.902Z",codex-agent,"Re-review rule: mutation plans must distinguish their own ordered writes from foreign target revisions, and preview/apply/replay/compensation must share that target identity contract. The supplied blocking case repeats an existing key, so each row currently captures the same base revision and mistakes the preceding row for an interleaving writer. Main is already an ancestor of this branch (zero commits behind), so no merge is needed. Auditing all native revision checks, atomic journals, update ownership comparisons and command/importer dispatch; regression coverage will include repeated-key aliases, ordering, replay, compensation/recovery, peer edits and packed npm/Bun consumers. Only one finding was supplied and public review threads contain no additional code findings."
  "2026-10-29T08:48:58.720Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed: both command/importer aliases dispatch through importCSV; admitted atomic steps now share ordered progress per canonical native target, including nonadjacent rows and distinct provenance-key aliases. Preview, application, replay and reverse compensation read the same SDK-verified target progress and recheck the current checkpoint before each write. Ordinary/streaming/legacy atomic imports and negotiated tables use the sequential mutation core; spreadsheet sessions and join plans reject duplicate canonical IDs before application; lineage uses row-specific identities. Atomic-update ownership comparisons also incorrectly treated SDK explicit-unset suffixes as foreign; every comparison now uses the shared message normalizer. Five focused regressions pass across ordered native transitions, every row failure/peer boundary, all status roles, normalized audit phases and negotiated table updates. Packed current-host tests now check repeated-target JSON/TOON apply, replay and SDK-backed export in all six launcher contexts."
  "2026-10-29T08:58:22.187Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof completed in a disposable non-git package copy with real temporary trackers: the fixed baseline passed; reverting only importCSVAtomicInternal failed the repeated lifecycle/target regression; reverting only compensateUpdate failed the released explicit-unset audit regression; reverting only inspectUpdate failed that inspection regression. Each restored function passed its selected test again, and all reviewed source hashes stayed unchanged. The first audit fixture exposed a host-version distinction: the pinned older host does not generate the newer explicit-unset suffix itself. The must-allow fixture now passes the released message shape through a real native CLI write, while packed current-host tests exercise actual scope-clear production. The preliminary linked test run failed only that superseded fixture assumption (5 passed, 1 failed); the corrected linked run will be recorded separately, with no tracker policy changes."
  "2026-10-29T09:05:10.717Z",codex-agent,"Corrected linked regression run passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 900 --shared-host-safe --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run: 6 tests passed, zero failures/skips/cancellations. The broader focused native regression/coverage run passed 12 tests with zero skips; every newly changed admission/index branch was exercised. Existing unrelated branches outside that focused selection remain delegated to the full release gate, with thresholds unchanged. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks passed. The six new cases cover 16 generated ordered sequences across import engines, twelve row-boundary failure/peer interleavings, custom lifecycle roles, released audit shape compatibility, negotiated tables and interrupted compensation recovery. Test fixtures enforce a non-git ceiling. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI after this review fix; the previously reviewed head already completed both runtimes and managers successfully."
  "2026-10-29T09:17:02.202Z",codex-agent,"Final class coverage also applies ordered checkpoints to single existing-target updates, so own rollback/retry semantics are consistent instead of being special-cased for duplicates. Admitted dry-run now refuses pending compensation before it can label restored rows unchanged. Five additional focused cases passed (including single-target rollback/retry, interrupted recovery with a read-only dry-run refusal, existing replay guards and custom lifecycle roles). npm run accept:packed passed all nine scenarios, including repeated-target apply/replay and JSON/TOON SDK-backed state checks in all six current-host launcher contexts. The original public-copy and million-row evidence is retained rather than rerun: these changes affect target checkpoint/ownership handling, not streaming admission allocations. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates now require fresh CI for this fix. No extra non-blocking review findings were present in the supplied instruction, queue review task or public PR threads."
  "2026-10-29T09:17:36.243Z",codex-agent,"Final planner-only revert proof was repeated after extending the common checkpoint logic to single-target retries and pending-compensation dry-runs: restoring the pre-fix importCSVAtomicInternal in a disposable copy failed both repeated-target lifecycle and single-target rollback/retry cases (0 passed, 2 failed); restoring the fixed function passed both (2 passed, 0 failed). The prior compensateUpdate and inspectUpdate function-only mutants remain red against the released-message fixture, and their restored checks pass. Reviewed source hashes were unchanged by every proof. Final typecheck, lint, docstrings, zero-duplication and diff checks passed. No native history was rewritten."
  "2026-10-29T09:21:50.426Z",codex-agent,"Final linked run of node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/repeated-targets.test.ts passed all 7 tests, with zero failures/skips/cancellations, through pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 900 --shared-host-safe --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run (run test-local-mvtc1rza-ge8c1u). Existing policy disables automatic evidence persistence, so this receipt is recorded without changing policy. The additional same-plan peer case also verifies that a peer performs both repeated writes while the caller adopts the durable bindings, reports zero own updates and reads the final value through the SDK. The claim remains released; this final validation note precedes the CI commit."
  "2026-10-29T09:52:33.716Z",codex-agent,"Re-review CI handoff at the 30-minute monitoring cutoff: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/40849260194 checks implementation 6b0146c. Node 26 npm run release:check passed with unchanged 100% line/branch/function coverage and expanded packed acceptance; Node 26 Bun remains running. Node 22 npm remains running and its Bun gate is pending. No current full-job test counts are claimed before logs become downloadable. Local evidence: final linked regressions 7/7, broader focused selection 12/12, follow-up selection 5/5, same-plan peer scenario 1/1 and packed acceptance 9/9; three function-only mutants fail and restored checks pass. The supplied repeated-target finding and the related ownership/recovery class are fixed; no additional supplied/public non-blocking findings were found. This handoff changes only tracker evidence and requires a fresh final-head CI check. The item remains in progress with my claim released; no merge or publication."
